<title>GERMANY: ECONOMISTS' FORECASTS FOR MAY JOBLESS DATA.</title>
<headline>ECONOMISTS' FORECASTS FOR MAY JOBLESS DATA.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Economists polled by Reuters on Monday gave the following forecasts for May German jobless data which will be released on Friday.</p>
<p>All forecasts give the the absolute change expected in the seasonally-adjusted figure in May compared with April.</p>
<p>Economist				    5/97 vs.  5/97   yr 97</p>
<p>						 4/97	pct    pct</p>
<p>						 (s.a.)    (n.a.)</p>
<p>Christine Walter, Commerzbank	  + 5.000   10.8%  11.2%</p>
<p>Stefan Bergheim, Dresdner KB	   +-    0   11.0%  11.2%</p>
<p>Lothar Hessler, Trinkaus Cap.Mgmt.   - 5.000   11.0%  11.0%</p>
<p>Holger Fahringkrug, UBS	-15.000    n/a   11.2%</p>
<p>Armin Kayser, SBC Warburg		-15.000   11.2%  11.2%</p>
<p>Hans Jaeckel, DG Bank		    - 5.000   10.9%  11.2%</p>
<p>Nikolaus Keis, Bayer. Vereinsbank    - 5.000   11.0%  11.1%</p>
<p>Thomas Kull, Westdt. Landesbank	+-    0   10.9%  11.0%</p>
<p>Jens Kramer, Norddt. Landesbank	+ 5.000   10.9%  11.2%</p>
<p>Adolf Rosenstock, IBJ Deutschland    +10.000   10.9%  11.2%</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
